  "rationale": "Comparison for unit:shared.typing.expression_soundness against lean:Shared/TypingSafety:expression_soundness. The public expression_soundness theorem provides existence and realization for every Eval, appending the result to arbitrary pending values. Realizes entails the table/type prerequisites. The public signature has no residual expression-soundness axiom or assumed successful evaluation, so the prose's existence claim is supported. Notation and judgment context was checked in unit:shared.typing.realization, unit:shared.typing.expressions, unit:shared.typing.well_formed_classes, unit:shared.typing.erasure, unit:shared.steps. Rooted-foundation review: the structural invariants now require explicit rootedness (including pending values) plus unique/compatible ownership. Allocation bounds remain solely for freshness; no safety proof assumes edge-age order or global DAG structure. Changed proof selections retain their public statement unless this unit explicitly defines the revised invariant or example. Given/Shared root transport and path reasoning were reviewed by their implementing agents, with fresh review of root-owned unpacking, GC, frame rerooting, class retention and the refill example. Earlier syntax and runtime rules are unchanged. The widened invariant domain is covered by recompilation of all earlier safety proofs and concrete shared-cycle/nonmonotonic-ID regressions, not by a claim that constructors can generate cycles.",
